  "worked_solution": "We see that this is a geometric series with a common ratio of $r=\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}}.$\n\nFor the series to converge, we require $|r|<1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}}| & <1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{{81}^{k}} & <1 \\\\ 9 & <{81}^{k} \\\\ {81}^{k} & >9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we could remove the absolute value bars because $\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}}$ is always positive.\n\nThe equation ${81}^{k}=9$ has the solution $k=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Now, since ${81}^{k}$ increases as $k$ increases, the solution to ${81}^{k}>9$ must be $k>\\frac{1}{2}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
